            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for need, then the Telugu for an introduction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: తెలుగులో",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తెలుగులో (telugulō) — \"in Telugu\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is తెలుగు with -లో, \"in\", the ending you met on ఉండు. Any language takes it: ఇంగ్లీషులో, \"in English\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "తెలుగులో (telugulō) is native Dravidian: telugu, the language's name, which DEDR 3426 lists as teluṅgu, and -lō, \"in\", which DEDR 698 lists as lō, \"inside\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A way to name the language you want an answer in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
