        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ఎలా అంటారు?",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఎలా అంటారు? (elā aṇṭāru?) — \"how does one say it?\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "దీన్ని తెలుగులో (telugulō) ఎలా అంటారు? (elā aṇṭāru?) — \"how do you say this in Telugu?\". అను, \"to say\", is the verb inside అని and అనుకో."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Both words are native Dravidian: elā, \"how\" (DEDR 5151), and anu, \"to say\" (DEDR 868)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The one question that lets a learner learn from anyone."
            }
          ]
        },
